are has temporarily moved to VRCCO East due to renovations but we remain open for outpatient services.\n1820 NW Monterey Pines\nBend, Oregon 97703\n541-204-1261\nCALL NOW\nLEARN MORE\nVRCCO EAST\n24/7 Emergency\n& Specialty Hospital\n62889 NE Oxford Ct.\nBend, Oregon 97701\n541-209-6960\nCALL\nLEARN MORE\nVRCCO WEST\nUrgent Care &\nOutpatient Services\nUrgent Care has temporarily moved to VRCCO East due to renovations but we remain open for outpatient services.\n1820 NW Monterey Pines\nBend, Oregon\n541-204-1261\nCALL\nLEARN MORE\nBe Your Pet’s Hero\n®\nWith decades of devotion to the veterinary field, and a lifetime of being animal lovers, we know how important it is to be your pet’s hero. VRCCO offers exceptional, one of a kind service for our pet parents and patient-guests. We strive to make real connections with our community in order to deliver the best experience and animal healthcare.\nABOUT VRCCO\n24/7 Emergency Care\nEquipped to handle any type of pet emergency at any time. No appointment necessary.\nSpecialty Care\nA wide range of services with support from our collaborative team of board-certified specialists.\nUrgent Care\nFor Cases that aren’t emergent, our urgent care center offers non-critical same day care.\nWhat Pet Parents Say\nVeterinary Specialties\nOur board-certified, highly trained doctors and staff offer expertise in every area of advanced veterinary care. Together we provide the most sophisticated and responsive support to you and your pet.\nBONE, JOINT, SPINE\nAdvancing the standard of orthopedic and neurologic surgical care.\nExplore\nSURGERY\nBoard-certified expertise from the operating room to the recovery room.\nExplore\nONCOLOGY\nAdvanced, comprehensive oncologic care for your pets.\nExplore\nDermatology & Allergy\nFind comfort and relief for your pet through tailored treatment plans.\nExplore\nOphthalmology\nDiagnosing and treating conditions affecting the eyes.\nExplore\ninternal medicine\nThe diagnosis, pathology, and treatment of internal body systems.\nExplore\nneurology\nTreating nervous system disorders involving the brain, spinal cord, nerves & muscles.\nExplore\nRehabilitation Therapy\nRegaining your pet’s strength and function.\nExplore\nJoin Our Team\nVeterinary Jobs at VRCCO\nIf you are interested in working in a dynamic environment with passionate team members, view our open positions to see if there is a good fit for your experience.\nLEARN MORE\nLocally Owned, Community-Connected\nOur Passion is Delivering Exceptional Experiences with Unparalleled Care\nVet cadets\nChildcare Center at VRCCO\nPonch's Place\nFood truck & beverage pavilion\nEvents\nVRCCO Event Calendar\nLearning Institute\nContinuing Education\nBlood Bank\nHelp Save Lifes\nPetsForward\nDonate to Pets in Need\nJoin Our Community\nGet our latest on community events, learning and veterinary news.\nEmail Address\nSign Up\nEMERGENCY\n541-209-6960\nDirections\nSPECIALTY CARE\n541-209-6960\nDirections\nURGENT CARE\n541-204-1261\nDirections\nFAQ GUIDE\nEverything you\nneed to know.\nCARE\nEmergency\nSpecialty Care\nUrgent Care Center\nBone, Joint & Spine Center\nABOUT\nHospital\nAbout VRCCO\nOur Team\nVet Cadets Childcare\nDonations\nCOMMUNITY\nVet Cadets Childcare\nEvent Calendar\nPonch's Place Food\nLearning Institute\nCONTACT\nContact Us\nPrivacy Policy\nMain Hospital\n62889 NE Oxford Ct.\nBend, Oregon 97701\n541-209-6960\nUrgent Care Center\n1820 NW Monterey Pines\nBend, Oregon 97703\n541-204-1261\n©Copyright 2026 VRCCO. Website by\nZoePDX",
